# Closeout - exact manual package M0-M8 acceptance

Normative contract accepted through conditional owner authority and official executor approval of exact registration. M0-M8 and only their hash-pinned metadata definitions are incorporated; original proposal/earlier accepted decisions remain unchanged. Original Windows-1252 clause bytes are preserved in a frozen authoritative annex; the new registration is UTF8. No transcoded text is mislabeled byte-exact.

[Accepted record](../../adr/DECISION-manual-package-m0-m8-20261020.md) · [Sixteen-condition and compatibility review](conformance-matrix.md) · [Byte ranges/hashes](preimages-and-incorporation.json) · [Hashes](final-manifest.json).

The suite/encoding/bounds are accepted as normative choices, NOT as backend/target/implementation qualification. NT4/VC6, selected vetted PBKDF2/crypto adapters, KDF responsiveness/cancellation, Browser full import and the transitive ED11/native peak remain hard gates. The existing Browser advanced path stays intact. No code, builds, tests, packages, keys, certificates, private signing, network or CURRENT publication occurred.

The next authorized implementation request can start with bounded offline envelope/ZIP/TLV preparation and denial paths using the same owners. Any secret/crypto adapter integration still requires vetted artifact selection and exact functional review; no primitive is invented, no parameter is tuned, and missing actual authority denies operational generation. No additional normative change is required merely to repeat the already accepted suite; a real incompatibility requires a specific subsequent review rather than silent fallback.

